{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518576-average-age-for-first-change","id":518576,"title":"Average age for First Change?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-18T17:14:59-07:00","id":518576,"title":"Average age for First Change?","content":"Still familiarizing myself with 2nd Edition... warming up to WtF a little more. I think my perspective was just colored from having played WtA for so long. Trying to look at it with a fresh set of eyes. That said, I can't seem to find this anywhere. If memory serves me, in 1st Edition, they leave much more leaway for when the First Change can occur (as opposed to just shortly after puberty, like WtA). Don't see it mentioned anywhere in 2nd Edition, unless I'm missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6039-mattlutz","name":"MattLutz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T17:31:10-07:00","id":518606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MattLutz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518576-average-age-for-first-change#post518576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still familiarizing myself with 2nd Edition... warming up to WtF a little more. I think my perspective was just colored from having played WtA for so long. Trying to look at it with a fresh set of eyes. That said, I can't seem to find this anywhere. If memory serves me, in 1st Edition, they leave much more leaway for when the First Change can occur (as opposed to just shortly after puberty, like WtA). Don't see it mentioned anywhere in 2nd Edition, unless I'm missing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, that's left up to the Storyteller. The &quot;official&quot; answer, I think, would be that it's too varied to find a reliable average, but nWoD is a toolbox, so if you want to say most Uratha First Change as teenagers in your games (just as an example), go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T17:53:39-07:00","id":518616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MattLutz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518576-average-age-for-first-change#post518576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still familiarizing myself with 2nd Edition... warming up to WtF a little more. I think my perspective was just colored from having played WtA for so long. Trying to look at it with a fresh set of eyes. That said, I can't seem to find this anywhere. If memory serves me, in 1st Edition, they leave much more leaway for when the First Change can occur (as opposed to just shortly after puberty, like WtA). Don't see it mentioned anywhere in 2nd Edition, unless I'm missing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you could have 11 years old or 33 years old, to 57 years old changing. No rhyme or reason. Just the way Luna likes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T04:40:12-07:00","id":519412,"title":"","content":"I think late teens is the average, but it's just that: the <i>average</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:17:20-07:00","id":519544,"title":"","content":"There are examples in First edition of people experiencing their First Change at age 10 and age 55. Both cases were remarked upon as outliers. I don't believe the rules have changed, but generally I remember the book saying that most people experience it sometime after the onset of puberty but before the infirmity of old age. But even that is just most people. Late teens might be the average, but like everyone said, it's really up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:10:32-07:00","id":550078,"title":"","content":"In the books there are several instances of werewolf parents who pretty much give up hope that their wolf-blooded children will become werewolves themselves if they haven't Changed by their early twenties, often resulting in abandonment or relegation to breeding stock. So I'd say middle teens to early twenties, with plenty of exceptions in either direction for it never to be a sure thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2576-andrewsharp","user":"AndrewSharp","date":". 06-11-2015, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2576-andrewsharp","name":"AndrewSharp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}